    {
      "datasource": { "type": "datasource", "uid": "grafana" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 22 },
      "id": 6,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "markdown",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "### Trace control\n\n1. Open **Tempo Explore** (top link) filtered by `$service`.\n2. Click a **Trace ID** → waterfall of real API/Automation flow steps.\n3. Copy the Trace ID into the **Trace ID** variable above to filter logs.\n4. Or click the derived **TraceID** field on any log line.\n\n**Structured log fields**\n- Correlation: `trace_id`, `request_id`, `user_id`, and `service` at the top level.\n- Event details: `context`; Loki `| json` extracts `context_event`, `context_route`, `context_outcome`, and `context_latency_ms`.\n- Exceptions: `error.name`, sanitized `error.message`, `error.stack`, and bounded `error.cause` chains.\n\n**Real path only**\n- Spans: `exportOtlpSpan` from API/Automation flow recorders → Tempo `:4318`\n- Logs: `@meltiply/observability` `log()` → one JSON console line + identical Loki line `:3100` (local/test)\n- No seed/demo data. Empty panels mean no Worker traffic in range.\n\n| Endpoint | Port |\n| --- | --- |\n| Grafana | 3001 |\n| Tempo OTLP | 4318 |\n| Tempo query | 3200 |\n| Loki | 3100 |\n",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "How to drive this board",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
